CREATE article:getting_started_with_laravel_queues SET author = user:hannah_s, slug = "getting-started-with-laravel-queues", title = "Getting started with Laravel queues", description = "The trick is to make the right thing the easy thing. Nothing replaces talking to the people who use what you build.", body = "Measure first, then decide what to optimise. Constraints in the database outlive every application that talks to it. Every abstraction leaks eventually; plan for it. Readable code is cheaper than clever code.

Your future self is the most important reader of your code. Start with the smallest change that could possibly work. Naming matters more than we like to admit. Defaults shape behaviour far more than documentation does.

